.TH heliosctl-uplinks 1 0.3.0 "heliosctl 0.3.0" "Helios Manual"
.SH NAME
heliosctl\-uplinks \- A device\*(Aqs network interfaces: addresses, routes, its public address checks, and which uplinks its SRTLA bonds use or hold in standby
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBheliosctl uplinks\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-public\-addresses\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDEVICE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
A device\*(Aqs network interfaces: addresses, routes, its public address checks, and which uplinks its SRTLA bonds use or hold in standby
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON document on stdout, and errors as JSON on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-public\-addresses\fR
Also show each uplink\*(Aqs public IPv4 address. Off by default: it\*(Aqs personal data (it locates the connection), so keep it out of logs and anything shared
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL (…/dev)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
The AWS profile: one that assumes helios\-operator [default: helios\-operator]
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
The AWS region [default: the profile\*(Aqs]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDEVICE\fR>
A device ID (d\-…) or thing name (t\-…)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBheliosctl\fR(1), for exit status, environment, files and security.
